feat(shipwright): register 5 retool ships + ADR-0032 unSpider, cartographer, spider — archetype catalog 12 → 20

The 2026-05-20 fleet retool added five new ships (code-reviewer, red-team,
test-author, tautology-sniffer, tenderfoot) and the operator promoted
cartographer out of fleet-only into a first-class archetype. ADR-0031's
Spider and ADR-0032's unSpider — proposed but never landed — finally
register as real entries. The closed catalog grows from twelve to twenty.

Pairs: code-reviewer↔red-team (critical pair on PR open/sync),
test-author↔tautology-sniffer (generative/critical pair on PR open),
spider↔unspider (generative/critical pair on the roadmap surface).
Tenderfoot — the renamed retool-era "unspider," outside-in onboarding
critic — is observational and sui generis. Cartographer is its own
cartographic family because it's the only archetype that writes to the
planning surfaces.

The Archetype interface gained eight optional retool fields (family,
pairsWith, description, triggers, outputs, costClass, backendDefault,
backendEscalation). Existing twelve entries default to family
'maintenance' via archetypeFamily() — no behavior change. TriggerKind
grew four new kinds (pull-request-merged, cartographer-write,
sortie-completed, claim-acquired) to back the new event-driven
archetypes. New ARCHETYPES export holds the canonical roster ordered
family → alphabetical: generative, critical, maintenance, observational,
cartographic.

Companion work in pd-fleet.yml and fleet/ships/*.md (renaming the
retool-era "unspider" to "tenderfoot", runtime backend detection) is
owned by session-fleet-retool-corrections — that diff is intentionally
out of scope here. Shipwright-changed channel notified for downstream
consumers (note id 58814).

On the augur question: the operator asked whether ADR-0032's unSpider
deserved a better name (augur was suggested — Roman priest who divined
from contradictions, perfect cathedral analogy). Deferred. The
in-flight fleet-retool-corrections session already locked in
"unspider" = ADR-0032 and "tenderfoot" = retool ship, so renaming
unspider → augur now would create more confusion than it resolves.
Worth revisiting once that branch lands.

Validation:
  tsc --noEmit: clean
  jest tests/unit/shipwright-archetypes.test.js: 18/18 pass (was 12)
  jest tests/unit/: 5846 pass / 1 skipped (zero regressions)


